GEOMETRY NOTES (world-space scale, color palette, and any formula/value needed for correctness — build to these so sizes, zoom, and colors match the source; do not guess dimensions the notes already specify):
World scale: each embedding plane is a flat 4 × 4 unit square lying in the XZ plane (drawn as a parallelogram under the isometric pose), with a faint 4×4 grid (#e2e2e2, 1px) and a dark outline #4a4a4a, ~2.5px. Five planes per branch stacked along +Y with 2.6 unit spacing, so plane centers at y = 0, 2.6, 5.2, 7.8, 10.4. Image branch centered at x = -4.5, text branch at x = +4.5; both share the same z = 0 center and identical plane sizes. Orange disk: radius 1.0, centered at (0, 13.6, 0), fill #F5A882, black outline 2px, label 'Joint embedding space' in serif above it. Black arrows from (-4.5,11.0) and (+4.5,11.0) angling inward to the disk edge. Between consecutive left planes a vertical black arrow at x = -7.6 (shaft ~1.8 units, solid black, filled head up); the rounded white box 'ViT block x3' (monospace text, 1px black border, radius 0.3) sits centered on that arrow's midpoint at x = -7.6. Mirrored on the right at x = +7.6 with 'transformer block x3'. Far-left vertical rule at x = -10.5 spanning y = -0.5 to 12, with rotated serif label 'Image encoder'; far-right rule at x = +10.5 with 'Text encoder'. Ten concepts, each with one persistent color: red circle #EF6A6A, orange circle #F5B267, pink circle #F48FB1, purple circle #B39DDB, blue circle #64B5F6, pink square #F06BB4, blue square #7EC8E3, green square #66BB6A, blue triangle #4FA8D8, purple triangle #A48AD0. Markers are ~0.18-unit glyphs (circle/square/triangle) drawn on the plane surface with matching fill and slightly darker stroke. On the left, every plane holds the same 10 markers at different (x,z) positions; bottom plane positions are spread toward the plane's right/front, and positions progressively tighten into two or three color/shape clusters by the top plane. Dashed trajectory lines (dash 0.12/0.12, opacity 0.45) connect each marker to its counterpart on the plane above, in the concept's own color. On the right, the same 10 concepts appear as small dark serif text strings placed on each plane, connected by dashed gray lines #8a8a8a at opacity 0.4; some right-branch strings sit outside the plane outline near its left and right corners, as in the source. Highlighted concept: its marker and text grow ~1.5×, its dashed path goes opacity 1.0 and width 2, everything else drops to opacity 0.12.

